Why two licences
----------------

Apache 2.0 is a software licence. Its terms are written about source code,
object code, and patent grants, and they map poorly onto a diagram and a set
of written definitions. CC BY-SA 4.0 is designed for exactly this kind of
work: it is the standard licence for open educational resources, it is what
Wikipedia uses, and it is unambiguous about attribution and derivative works.


